WEBVTT

00:11.950 --> 00:13.320
Oh, no!

00:13.960 --> 00:16.840
You've done it now, Kugisaki.

00:16.840 --> 00:19.280
This was Gojo-sensei's, right?

00:25.420 --> 00:30.760
Ijichi-san.

00:25.640 --> 00:30.320
Between Ijichi-san, who left us in 
charge of this freshly cleaned shirt,

00:30.760 --> 00:32.760
Me ♥

00:30.860 --> 00:32.930
and me, who spilled coffee on it...

00:33.330 --> 00:34.510
Who's more at fault?

00:34.510 --> 00:35.390
You.

00:37.010 --> 00:39.040
You pat it down, pat it down.

00:39.040 --> 00:40.270
I'm working on it!

00:48.240 --> 00:51.200
It kind of looks like a marimekko.

00:51.200 --> 00:52.940
Don't take apparel so lightly.

00:52.940 --> 00:55.520
Eh, I'm sure it's a cheap shirt, anyway.

00:55.520 --> 00:58.110
Fushiguro, look up the brand on the tag.

01:07.420 --> 01:09.780
A-After tax?

01:09.780 --> 01:11.070
Before tax.

01:11.070 --> 01:12.560
Is that even important?

01:14.080 --> 01:15.460
We have no choice.

01:15.460 --> 01:17.560
I'll put in 90,000.

01:17.560 --> 01:19.240
You can each put in 80,000.

01:19.240 --> 01:20.200
Huh?!

01:20.200 --> 01:21.380
Morning!

01:21.380 --> 01:23.970
Ijichi said you guys had my shirt?

01:25.440 --> 01:27.390
What's the matter, Megumi?

01:27.390 --> 01:28.810
Nothing.

01:57.080 --> 01:58.790
Kugisaki...

02:08.240 --> 02:10.560
I-I can't...

02:25.810 --> 02:27.080
I'm thrilled!

02:27.390 --> 02:29.410
By my own talent!

02:29.410 --> 02:32.620
Ah, I really am...

02:32.620 --> 02:34.530
I truly am...

02:34.880 --> 02:36.880
a curse!

02:40.000 --> 02:41.350
Black Flash!

02:47.580 --> 02:49.280
I bet you just thought

02:49.280 --> 02:51.560
this would be some pest extermination,

02:51.560 --> 02:54.740
or like defeating evil spirits in a legend,

02:57.080 --> 03:00.550
or something like that 
when you came here, right?!

03:01.030 --> 03:04.210
You're naïve! You damn brat!

03:04.210 --> 03:07.080
This is war!

03:07.080 --> 03:10.510
It's not some fight to correct a mistake!

03:10.510 --> 03:13.300
It's a clash of what we believe is right!

03:13.300 --> 03:17.540
Of our own flimsy ideas of justice!

03:22.100 --> 03:25.760
You are me, Yuji Itadori.

03:30.080 --> 03:33.810
Just as I kill people 
without a second thought,

03:34.400 --> 03:38.800
you save people without a second thought!

03:38.800 --> 03:40.650
It's our instincts

03:40.650 --> 03:44.080
versus the dignity 
gained by human reasoning!

03:44.080 --> 03:50.200
This is a war to determine which of those 
will be left standing a century from now!

03:51.290 --> 03:55.160
If you haven't even realized that yet,

03:55.160 --> 03:57.580
how are you supposed to beat me?

04:03.070 --> 04:05.590
Hey, Yuji Itadori.

04:06.330 --> 04:09.190
Have you counted how 
many curses you've killed?

04:11.600 --> 04:13.330
I bet not.

04:13.330 --> 04:14.720
Me, neither!

04:15.080 --> 04:19.230
I really couldn't care less about 
the number of humans I've killed.

04:20.530 --> 04:24.870
Eventually, I'll forget all about you, too.

04:33.620 --> 04:37.470
The bells of the Gion monastery in India

04:38.200 --> 04:41.480
echo with the warning that 
all things are impermanent.

04:42.630 --> 04:45.960
The blossoms of the sala trees 
teach us through their hues

04:47.200 --> 04:51.160
that what flourishes must fade.

04:52.560 --> 04:54.060
However!

04:57.870 --> 05:00.940
We are the exception!

05:02.940 --> 05:05.940
Episode 44
Right and Wrong, Part 3

05:16.500 --> 05:21.020
JUJUTSU KAISEN
Shibuya Incident

06:35.950 --> 06:39.160
23:09            Tokyo Metro, Shibuya Station
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hFloor B5, Shin-toshin Line Platform

06:37.200 --> 06:38.810
These people...

06:39.160 --> 06:41.670
Kyoto School First-Year, Arata Nitta

06:39.890 --> 06:41.680
are alive, right?

06:47.480 --> 06:52.390
It looks like Suguru Geto has 
already left with the Prison Realm.

06:52.390 --> 06:53.760
No way!

06:54.640 --> 06:56.220
Let's switch gears.

06:56.720 --> 06:59.760
Our goal has changed from 
fighting to reclaim Satoru Gojo

06:59.760 --> 07:05.120
to fighting to save our allies and shave away 
as much of the enemy forces as possible,

07:05.120 --> 07:08.620
starting right now!

07:10.240 --> 07:11.530
Let's hurry.

07:11.530 --> 07:14.420
My brother should already be nearby.

07:15.440 --> 07:17.460
He has a brother?

07:17.460 --> 07:19.910
I could have sworn he was an only child.

07:24.010 --> 07:26.020
What just happened?

07:26.550 --> 07:28.260
A face with a scar!

07:28.260 --> 07:30.660
Plus the way he switched places just now!

07:30.660 --> 07:33.000
Is he the sorcerer who 
drove Hanami into a corner?!

07:33.000 --> 07:34.210
Todo-san!

07:34.210 --> 07:36.570
I finished treating that girl over there.

07:36.570 --> 07:38.850
She's probably dead, though.

07:38.850 --> 07:41.380
So please don't blame me later!

07:41.380 --> 07:43.020
Enough prattle.

07:43.020 --> 07:44.510
See to my brother, too.

07:44.510 --> 07:46.440
Wake up, Brother!

07:46.440 --> 07:49.010
Our battle has just begun!

07:49.010 --> 07:50.280
Talk about ominous lines!

07:52.200 --> 07:54.970
Todo...

07:56.920 --> 07:58.500
I...

07:58.990 --> 08:00.290
can't...

08:02.710 --> 08:04.290
fight anymore!

08:05.550 --> 08:08.120
It wasn't just Kugisaki...

08:08.120 --> 08:09.600
Nanamin died, too.

08:11.160 --> 08:15.160
Sukuna... killed so many.

08:15.160 --> 08:19.510
So I have to save...

08:19.510 --> 08:22.270
that many more people...

08:23.350 --> 08:25.470
But I couldn't!

08:25.470 --> 08:27.960
I'm just a murderer!

08:28.360 --> 08:33.360
What I thought was my conviction

08:34.180 --> 08:37.360
was just an excuse I made for myself!

08:41.860 --> 08:45.540
I can't...

08:47.020 --> 08:49.440
forgive myself anymore.

08:50.380 --> 08:54.200
Speak up! I can't hear you!

09:11.110 --> 09:12.360
Amazing!

09:12.360 --> 09:15.160
Even when you know about it, 
it's still this disorienting?!

09:15.880 --> 09:17.550
Brother...

09:17.550 --> 09:21.410
A man as great as you shouldn't 
let yourself grow so small.

09:21.740 --> 09:24.150
We are jujutsu sorcerers.

09:24.550 --> 09:25.670
Me,

09:25.670 --> 09:27.170
you,

09:27.170 --> 09:28.550
Kugisaki,

09:28.550 --> 09:30.150
Mr. Nanami,

09:30.540 --> 09:35.190
and all of our allies are jujutsu sorcerers!

09:36.040 --> 09:38.330
So long as we continue to live,

09:38.330 --> 09:40.440
our dead comrades

09:40.440 --> 09:43.680
have not truly been defeated!

09:44.200 --> 09:47.070
This is not a matter of sins 
and punishments.

09:47.400 --> 09:50.690
The moment we chose to 
live as jujutsu sorcerers,

09:50.690 --> 09:56.200
our lives were no longer 
bound by such karma.

09:56.520 --> 10:00.720
Attempting to find meaning 
in the deaths of the fallen

10:00.720 --> 10:03.960
can, at times, defile the 
memories of those we've lost!

10:04.710 --> 10:05.960
But even so!

10:07.940 --> 10:10.720
What have they entrusted you with?

10:14.430 --> 10:17.600
There's no need to find 
your answer to that now.

10:17.860 --> 10:20.250
But until you do,

10:20.250 --> 10:22.470
you cannot stop moving forward.

10:23.010 --> 10:26.360
That is the one punishment imposed

10:26.360 --> 10:28.370
on those who live as jujutsu sorcerers.

10:30.370 --> 10:34.850
There's no need to tell my brother 
about that right now.

10:42.950 --> 10:45.370
I've applied my technique to you.

10:45.370 --> 10:47.420
Now, listen up, Itadori-kun.

10:47.860 --> 10:51.800
The wounds you have suffered 
so far will no longer worsen.

10:52.210 --> 10:53.700
They are {i}not{/i} healed,

10:53.700 --> 10:56.560
but you'll stop losing blood, 
and it should take the edge off the pain.

10:56.560 --> 10:59.000
But that only applies 
to your current wounds.

10:59.650 --> 11:02.410
If you take another attack, 
you'll be further wounded,

11:02.410 --> 11:06.090
and my technique won't apply to those.

11:06.090 --> 11:09.060
Todo-san's little brother 
doesn't resemble him at all.

11:09.640 --> 11:12.640
I gave the girl over there 
the same treatment.

11:14.370 --> 11:16.540
She didn't have a pulse 
and wasn't breathing,

11:16.540 --> 11:18.300
but it hadn't been very long.

11:18.300 --> 11:20.420
The chance that she survives isn't zero.

11:21.180 --> 11:24.150
I'm taking her with me 
and getting out of here.

11:24.520 --> 11:26.410
I'm just saying the chance isn't zero!

11:26.410 --> 11:28.610
Please don't get your hopes up too high!

11:30.560 --> 11:31.540
Yeah...

11:32.790 --> 11:33.810
Yeah!

11:34.410 --> 11:37.920
Are you finished talking, topknot gorilla?

12:27.300 --> 12:28.810
What's wrong?

12:28.810 --> 12:31.060
You won't touch me?

12:31.840 --> 12:33.670
He's skilled.

12:33.670 --> 12:38.140
He's parrying me while also keeping 
distance from the nearly finished Itadori.

12:38.500 --> 12:41.350
That's not all I've got.

12:43.820 --> 12:45.340
He dodged it?

12:45.340 --> 12:47.440
Bring on the switch!

12:47.440 --> 12:48.920
This time, I'll adapt!

12:48.920 --> 12:50.620
I'll hit him for sure!

12:51.290 --> 12:54.080
I want to land that thing once more!

12:54.440 --> 12:57.330
I can feel myself close to reaching it!

12:57.680 --> 13:00.950
The true essence of my soul!

13:05.000 --> 13:07.150
I'm sorry, Nanamin.

13:08.120 --> 13:09.860
I was trying to take the easy way out.

13:10.650 --> 13:14.600
I even used my sins as an excuse to run away.

13:17.950 --> 13:19.800
Please take it from here.

13:20.770 --> 13:22.570
Black Flash!

13:32.500 --> 13:37.510
I'll make sure I take on your 
share of suffering, too, Nanamin.

13:43.410 --> 13:46.380
Tsk! Half-dead boy!

13:55.490 --> 13:57.100
Welcome back.

13:57.600 --> 13:58.240
Yeah!

14:00.020 --> 14:04.030
Shibuya Station Closed Off

14:07.510 --> 14:10.120
Matters should be settled already.

14:10.120 --> 14:13.240
There's no point in going to Shibuya now.

14:13.550 --> 14:16.280
Head back, Miwa.

14:30.650 --> 14:33.930
Why only Todo-senpai and Nitta-kun?

14:33.930 --> 14:38.410
I reasoned there's a 99% chance 
that Todo won't die in Shibuya.

14:38.800 --> 14:41.860
Same for Nitta if he accompanied Todo.

14:41.860 --> 14:43.900
His technique would be useful, too—

14:43.900 --> 14:45.120
And me?!

14:49.870 --> 14:53.670
Am I useless?

14:58.290 --> 15:01.690
The situation isn't even 
on that scale anymore.

15:02.080 --> 15:03.780
It wasn't just you.

15:03.780 --> 15:08.150
It was Mai, Kamo, Nishimiya, 
and Utahime, too.

15:08.150 --> 15:13.220
I took steps to make sure you all were 
on a mission south of Kyoto on the 31st.

15:13.960 --> 15:16.140
Why didn't you say anything to us?

15:16.810 --> 15:19.480
Why didn't you ask us for help?

15:19.480 --> 15:22.030
Aren't we friends?

15:24.230 --> 15:25.720
Is it because...

15:26.160 --> 15:27.380
I'm weak?

15:27.380 --> 15:30.360
No. I'm the one who was weak.

15:31.530 --> 15:34.360
I went about it the wrong way 
because I was weak,

15:34.360 --> 15:38.620
and I couldn't even see that mistake 
through because I was weak.

15:45.470 --> 15:47.900
There was this girl I loved.

15:48.350 --> 15:50.900
And I didn't care what 
happened to the world

15:50.900 --> 15:53.640
as long as I could be at 
her side and protect her.

15:58.970 --> 16:01.600
Even if that girl didn't want me

16:02.680 --> 16:05.030
to be the one to protect her.

16:21.320 --> 16:23.160
Time's up, Miwa.

16:23.160 --> 16:23.880
No!

16:24.790 --> 16:27.280
Goodbye. Thank you—

16:27.280 --> 16:29.200
Don't say goodbye!

16:30.360 --> 16:31.190
Miwa.

16:31.250 --> 16:32.300
Mechamaru!

16:32.300 --> 16:33.180
Miwa!

16:35.140 --> 16:36.980
Please find happiness.

16:39.270 --> 16:43.180
Whatever shape it takes,
as long as you're happy,

16:43.180 --> 16:45.430
my wish has come true.

16:51.270 --> 16:52.690
Mechamaru...

17:04.920 --> 17:08.460
Utahime-sensei, what Mechamaru did...

17:08.460 --> 17:09.950
Will go unquestioned.

17:09.950 --> 17:11.800
The man is dead, after all.

17:12.210 --> 17:15.340
He held us in awfully low regard, huh?

17:16.050 --> 17:16.960
Right?

17:16.960 --> 17:19.590
And this whole "Todo-kun wouldn't die" crap?

17:19.590 --> 17:22.600
Is he saying that we would die, then?

17:23.450 --> 17:27.390
I'll murder whoever 
makes my cute junior cry.

17:43.650 --> 17:45.790
He can switch positions 
with inanimate objects?!

18:07.600 --> 18:08.730
He split apart!

18:23.380 --> 18:25.160
Soul Multiplicity!

18:25.160 --> 18:26.000
Body Repel!

18:44.680 --> 18:48.640
Topknot Gorilla's soul is 
still at full strength,

18:48.640 --> 18:51.510
but could I kill him with 
one touch in my current state?

18:52.110 --> 18:56.260
Itadori's soul is down to about 10% left.

18:56.910 --> 19:00.600
And my soul is down to 40%.

19:01.280 --> 19:04.030
Having my double crushed

19:04.030 --> 19:07.690
and eating Itadori's rush of 
Black Flashes shaved away an awful lot.

19:08.040 --> 19:11.840
And that's all thanks to that woman.

19:11.840 --> 19:15.640
She was a nobody, but she 
still left her damn mark behind.

19:16.170 --> 19:19.720
I'll start by eliminating 
this annoying switcher first!

20:47.920 --> 20:49.180
Brother!

20:56.520 --> 20:59.200
If you're satisfied with 
staying on that level,

20:59.200 --> 21:02.440
you and I won't stay best friends.

21:03.410 --> 21:07.560
This cursed spirit is already 
landing Black Flash, too...

21:07.910 --> 21:11.280
I'm the one being left behind right now.

21:11.280 --> 21:14.000
You've grown strong, Brother.

21:14.000 --> 21:16.460
Are you satisfied with that,

21:16.460 --> 21:18.160
Aoi Todo?!

21:18.160 --> 21:21.400
Are you planning to leave 
your brother alone once again,

21:21.400 --> 21:23.290
Aoi Todo?!

21:42.980 --> 21:45.950
Tan-taka-tan!

21:46.440 --> 21:48.360
Black Flash!

21:58.200 --> 22:00.750
It doesn't matter how 
powerful your attack is,

22:00.750 --> 22:02.580
or if you throw out a Black Flash.

22:02.580 --> 22:07.040
Your attacks don't affect my soul, 
so they're pointless.

22:15.990 --> 22:21.000
However, with that, 
all three of them were now...

22:21.920 --> 22:22.720
Smooch!

22:22.340 --> 22:28.320
Smooch♥

22:22.720 --> 22:27.760
...drawing out 120% of their latent potential.

22:34.200 --> 22:36.040
Soul Multiplicity!

22:36.200 --> 22:37.590
Body Repel!

22:40.160 --> 22:43.580
An omnidirectional attack 
that makes switching pointless!

22:43.580 --> 22:46.120
He's getting into high gear!

23:15.240 --> 23:18.120
Let's kick it up a notch, Itadori!

23:18.120 --> 23:20.000
This will be the last time

23:20.000 --> 23:23.750
you and I curse each other!

23:25.510 --> 23:28.530
They say a hero always arrives late,

23:28.530 --> 23:31.690
but everyone understands 
that those who worked hard

23:31.690 --> 23:34.340
and held out are heroes, too, right?

23:34.340 --> 23:36.430
Next time, "Metamorphosis."

23:34.600 --> 23:39.890
Next Episode
Metamorphosis

23:36.430 --> 23:39.520
Don't forget to grab your delay certificate!
